  "summary": {
   "status": "complete",
   "text": "Kevin Warsh described the current wave of artificial intelligence as potentially the most productivity-enhancing wave of our lifetimes. In July 2026 testimony, he said the rapid and apparently accelerating pace reflects data center construction and demand for AI-related equipment and software. He also said the extent of the economy's benefit from the AI buildout is unknown, while noting that the Federal Reserve is monitoring implications for inflation and the labor market. Warsh stated that strong productivity growth predated gains from AI adoption.",
   "sids": [
    "s1",
    "s2",
    "s3",
    "s4"
   ],
   "sentences": [
    {
     "text": "Kevin Warsh described the current wave of artificial intelligence as potentially the most productivity-enhancing wave of our lifetimes.",
